    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363-a1">

                <pb facs="0538" n="464" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg464"/>


                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Bustamente to Mr.
                        Prevost.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Quito,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 21, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, minister of exterior relations of Ecuador, has the honor to
                    inform the consul of the United States of the North that he has received his
                    note of the 26th of February last, and that by the next mail he will give the
                    required orders to satisfy his claim.</p>
                <p>Until then, the undersigned subscribes himself, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MANUEL BUSTAMENTE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. V. Prevost,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Consul,</hi> &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
